            <ArticleTitle>Insulin Resistance and Hunger in Childhood Obesity: A Patient and Physician's Perspective.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2386-2391</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12325-017-0606-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article is co-authored by the mother of a child with obesity and insulin resistance, who gives her perspective. It is also co-authored by the treating Obesity Medicine clinician and an investigator in obesity clinical research (both certified in Obesity Medicine), who give their perspectives. The discussion focuses upon the potential clinical use of metformin in managing young patients with obesity and insulin resistance. The article integrates what is scientifically known about the mechanisms of actions of metformin and how these mechanisms are reflected in the clinical response of young patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
